bug_report:
missing predicated VN  due to Canonical order of comparison with invariant
Take:
```
void foo(int);
void l(int**);
int f1(int j, int t)
{
  int p = 0;
  int *a = &p;
  l(&a);
  if (a == &p)
    return 0;
  for(int i = 0; i < j; i++)
  {
    if (a == &p) foo(p);
  }
  return 0;
}

```

We should be able to optimize out the call to foo because in the first iteration of the loop, a cannot be equal to `&p`.

But we don't record the predicate VN because the comparison is:
`&p == a.0_1`.

The patch which I put inPR 118867fixes this.
